[31m-## Official GSAP best practices[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- ✅ Use **property names in camelCase** in vars (e.g. `backgroundColor`, `rotationX`).[m
[31m-- ✅ Prefer **transform aliases** (`x`, `y`, `scale`, `rotation`, `xPercent`, `yPercent`, etc.) over animating the raw `transform` string; use **autoAlpha** instead of `opacity` for fade in/out when elements should be hidden and non-interactive at 0.[m
[31m-- ✅ Use documented built-in eases; use CustomEase only when a custom curve is needed.[m
[31m-- ✅ Store the tween/timeline return value when controlling playback (pause, play, reverse, kill).[m
[31m-- ✅ Prefer timelines instead of chaining animations using `delay`.[m
[31m-- ✅ Use **gsap.matchMedia()** for responsive breakpoints and **prefers-reduced-motion** so animations can be reduced or disabled for accessibility.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Do Not[m
[31m-[m
[31m-- ❌ Animate layout-heavy properties (e.g. `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`) when transform aliases (`x`, `y`, `scale`, `rotation`) can achieve the same effect; prefer transforms for better performance.[m
[31m-- ❌ Use both **svgOrigin** and **transformOrigin** on the same SVG element; only one applies.[m
[31m-- ❌ Rely on the default **immediateRender: true** when stacking multiple **from()** or **fromTo()** tweens on the same property of the same target; set **immediateRender: false** on the later tweens so they animate correctly.[m
[31m-- ❌ Use invalid or non-existent ease names; stick to documented eases.[m
[31m-- ❌ Forget that **gsap.from()** uses the element’s current state as the end state; the initial values in the tween will be applied immediately unless `immediateRender: false` is in the `vars`.[m
