[32m+[m[32m# Twodo[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32mTwodo is a task app built around **user experience first**. The interface stays deliberately simple on the surface, but the product is a **live experiment**: exploring the smoothest, most efficient ways to capture, organize, and finish work without fighting the UI.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## Design philosophy[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m**One-click mindset.** Flows are tuned so managing tasks takes as few steps as possible: direct controls, minimal navigation, and interactions that feel immediate rather than ceremonial.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m**Clarity over chrome.** The layout stays readable and purposeful so attention stays on what you are doing, not on deciphering the app.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## Core concepts[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Tasks** — Individual items you create, complete, filter, and archive in a focused workspace.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Projects** — A **project** is a shared container: a group of tasks that belong together (a product, a team initiative, or any bucket you choose).[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Collaboration** — You can **invite other people** into your project so everyone works from the same task list and context.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32mTogether, projects and invitations turn Twodo from a solo list into something you can run with others, still aligned with the same low-friction interaction model.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## Technical overview[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m| Area        | Stack |[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m|------------|--------|[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m| Frontend   | React (Vite), Tailwind CSS, MUI / Next UI, Framer Motion |[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m| Backend    | Node.js, Express |[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m| Data       | MongoDB (Mongoose) |[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m| Auth & extras | JWT-based API auth; Firebase-related configuration where used (e.g. storage) |[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32mRepository layout:[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- `frontend/twodo` — Vite React client[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m- `api` — Express API (`/api/todos`, `/api/projects`, `/api/invitations`, `/api/auth`, …)[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m## Local development[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **API** — From `api/`, install dependencies and start the server (e.g. `npm install` then `npm run dev` with nodemon, or `npm start`). Configure environment variables as required by your setup (for example `MONGODB_URI`, `JWT_SECRET`, and any Firebase-related variables used in `api/routes/firebaseConfig.js`).[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Frontend** — From `frontend/twodo/`, run `npm install` then `npm run dev`. By default the client targets `http://localhost:5000` for the API in development. You can override the base URL with `VITE_BASE_API_URL` if your API runs elsewhere.[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[41m[m
[32m+[m[32mTwodo is meant to feel fast and unobtrusive: **fewer clicks, clearer paths,** and room to refine what “efficient” means as the experiment continues.[m[41m[m
